From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SPX Kernel Integration <noreply@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8250: avoid parking MDP RCG at init

On SC8180X (Surface Pro X SQ1/SQ2), UEFI leaves the internal eDP panel
scanning out on disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src during handoff. Using
clk_rcg2_shared_ops parks the RCG at probe time before drm/msm takes over
the display pipeline.

Switch disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src to clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops
(exported by drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c in Linux 6.18), preserving
normal runtime enable/disable and s2idle parking behavior while leaving
the bootloader clock untouched during registration.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src = {
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_5,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_5),
 		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops,
 	},
 };
 
